# Shopify UI Guidelines

Core UI conventions for building Shopify-style admin apps using Shopify Polaris and TailwindCSS. These rules ensure a consistent, maintainable, and authentic Shopify look and feel while keeping the codebase simple and modern.

## Core Principles
- **KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid)** - Always choose the simplest, most maintainable solution
- **Shopify Look** - Always use Shopify Polaris components for UI elements to match Shopify admin style
- **Tailwind for Layout** - Always use TailwindCSS and semantic HTML tags for layout, spacing, and grouping
- **TypeScript First** - Always use TypeScript with strict typing (`strict: true`) everywhere
- **Less is More** - Always avoid unnecessary complexity, the best code is no code

## UI Elements
- Always use Shopify Polaris components for interactive and semantic UI elements:
  - `Button`, `TextField`, `Select`, `Badge`, `Card`, `Text`, `Icon`, `Banner`, etc.
- Always use these components for accessibility, keyboard support, and visual consistency with Shopify admin
- Never reimplement core UI elements that Polaris provides

✅ Good:
```tsx
<Button variant="primary">Save</Button>
<TextField label="Name" value={name} onChange={setName} />
<Card>
  <Text as="h2" variant="headingMd">Section</Text>
</Card>
```

❌ Bad:
```tsx
<button className="btn-primary">Save</button> // Wrong: Not using Polaris Button
<input type="text" /> // Wrong: Not using Polaris TextField
<div className="card">...</div> // Wrong: Not using Polaris Card
```

## Layout and Spacing
- Always use TailwindCSS utility classes and semantic HTML tags for layout, spacing, and grouping
- Never use Polaris layout primitives (`Box`, `BlockStack`, `InlineStack`, etc.) for layout or spacing
- Always use `div`, `section`, or other semantic tags with Tailwind for flex, grid, spacing, and alignment

✅ Good:
```tsx
<div className="flex items-center gap-4">
  <Text as="h2" variant="headingMd">Title</Text>
  <Badge>Active</Badge>
</div>
<div className="space-y-4">
  <TextField ... />
  <Button ... />
</div>
```

❌ Bad:
```tsx
<Box padding="400">...</Box> // Wrong: Use Tailwind for padding
<InlineStack gap="400">...</InlineStack> // Wrong: Use flex and gap in Tailwind
<BlockStack gap="400">...</BlockStack> // Wrong: Use flex-col and gap in Tailwind
```

## Reasoning
- Polaris UI elements guarantee a Shopify look, accessibility, and behavior
- Tailwind gives full control and consistency for layout, spacing, and responsiveness
- This approach keeps the codebase simple, modern, and easy to maintain

